{"id":"cb75cacbf4df8fe70ec64097dd57a4a6","question":"A load is pulled at uniform speed along a horizontal floor by a rope at 45° to the floor. If the force in the rope is 1500N, what is the frictional force?","prompt":"A load is pulled at uniform speed along a horizontal floor by a rope at 45° to the floor. If the force in the rope is 1500N, what is the frictional force?","options":{"a":"1524N","b":"1350N","c":"1260N","d":"1061N"},"correctAnswer":"d","explanation":"The horizontal component of the 1500N force at 45° is 1500 * cos(45°) ≈ 1061N. At uniform speed, this equals the frictional force.","subject":"Physics","normalizedSubject":"Physics","topic":null,"subtopic":null,"exam":"JAMB","examType":"JAMB","examYear":2012,"difficulty":null,"estimatedTime":null,"source":"SDASH","sourceName":"SdashAPI","sourceUrl":"https://sdashapi.com/api/v1/q","sourceMetadata":{"id":19274,"question":"A load is pulled at uniform speed along a horizontal floor by a rope at 45° to the floor. If the force in the rope is 1500N, what is the frictional force?","section":null,"passage":null,"option":{"a":"1524N","b":"1350N","c":"1260N","d":"1061N","e":""},"answer":"d","solution":"The horizontal component of the 1500N force at 45° is 1500 * cos(45°) ≈ 1061N. At uniform speed, this equals the frictional force.","image":null,"explanation_image":null,"examtype":"UTME","examyear":"2012","university":null},"provenance":[{"source":"SDASH","sourceName":"SdashAPI","sourceId":"19274","sourceUrl":"https://sdashapi.com/api/v1/q","rightsStatus":"USER_PROVIDED_AUTHORIZED","rightsEvidence":"User-provided authorization in the TUTOR-ME acquisition instructions."}],"rightsStatus":"USER_PROVIDED_AUTHORIZED","rightsEvidence":"User-provided authorization in the TUTOR-ME acquisition instructions.","verificationStatus":"pending","contentType":"multiple_choice","reviewedBy":null,"lastReviewedAt":null,"publishedAt":null,"createdAt":null,"updatedAt":null,"sourceId":"19274","contentHash":"f7e38c8780a10e399552fe810f59909